.\" gtk3sermo.1 — man page for gtk3sermo 1.0.0
.\" haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>
.\" This file is installed as /usr/share/man/man1/gtk3sermo.1
.\"
.TH GTK3DIALOG 1 "June 2026" "gtk3sermo 1.0.0" "haplo-dialog User Commands"
.SH NAME
gtk3sermo \- GTK3 dialog box creator for shell scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gtk3sermo
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B gtk3sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.br
.B gtk3sermo
\fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
.br
.B gtk3sermo
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
.br
.B VARIABLE=\(aq<window>...</window>\(aq gtk3sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gtk3sermo
reads a GTK3 GUI description written in an XML-like language and displays
the resulting dialog window. It is designed to be called from shell scripts
to present interactive forms, file choosers, progress bars, list views,
and other widgets without the script needing any knowledge of GTK
programming.
.PP
The GUI description can be supplied from an environment variable
.RB ( \-\-program ),
a file
.RB ( \-\-file ),
or standard input
.RB ( \-\-stdin ).
.PP
When a button action produces output (EXIT, REFRESH, etc.), gtk3sermo
prints the current value of each named widget to standard output in the
form
\fINAME\fR=\(dq\fIvalue\fR\(dq, which the calling shell can then
.BR eval .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug mode. Each character read from the dialog description is echoed
to standard output as it is fed to the lexer. Useful for diagnosing parser
issues.
.TP
.BI \-p " VARIABLE" "\fR,\fP \-\-program=" VARIABLE
Read the GUI description from the shell environment variable
.IR VARIABLE .
This is the most common invocation style in scripts:
.RS
.PP
.nf
MYGUI='<window>...</window>'
gtk3sermo --program=MYGUI
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BI \-f " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-file=" FILE
Read the GUI description from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-stdin
Read the GUI description from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-i " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-include=" FILE
Include and execute
.I FILE
before running the main GUI description.
.TP
.BI \-e " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-event-driven=" FILE
Execute
.I FILE
as an event-driven program. In this mode gtk3sermo acts as a dispatcher,
re-invoking
.I FILE
for each widget event.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-no-warning
Suppress non-fatal warning messages.
.TP
.BI \-G " GEOMETRY" "\fR,\fP \-\-geometry=" GEOMETRY
Set the initial window placement and size.
.I GEOMETRY
has the form
.RI [ W x H ][ + X + Y ]
following the X11 convention (e.g. \fB800x600+0+0\fR).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-center
Centre all windows on the screen.
.TP
.B \-\-print-ir
Parse the GUI description, print the internal representation, and exit
without displaying any window. Useful for debugging XML syntax errors.
.TP
.BI \-\-space-expand= STATE
Set the default
.I expand
packing state for all widgets.
.I STATE
is
.B true
or
.BR false .
.TP
.BI \-\-space-fill= STATE
Set the default
.I fill
packing state for all widgets.
.I STATE
is
.B true
or
.BR false .
.TP
.BI \-g " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-glade-xml=" FILE
Load a GtkBuilder UI file (.glade / .ui) instead of using the gtk3sermo
XML language.
.SH WIDGETS
gtk3sermo renders every widget with a native GTK 3 widget. The XML dialog
description language supports the following tags.
.SS Layout containers
.BR window ", " vbox ", " hbox ", " frame ", " notebook ", " expander ,
.BR eventbox ", " aspectframe
.SS Display widgets
.BR text ", " image ", " pixmap ", " statusbar ", " infobar ", " drawingarea
.SS Input widgets
.BR entry ", " edit ", " password ", " searchentry ", " spinbutton ", " hscale ,
.BR vscale ", " checkbox ", " togglebutton ", " radiobutton ", " switch
.SS Selection widgets
.BR combobox ", " comboboxtext ", " list ", " tree ", " table ", " colorbutton ,
.BR fontbutton ", " filechooser ", " calendar
.SS Progress and activity indicators
.BR progressbar ", " pulse ", " spinner ", " levelbar
.SS Button widgets
.BR button ", " linkbutton
.br
The
.B button
tag also accepts the stock short forms
.BR "button ok" ,
.BR "button cancel" ,
.BR "button help" ,
.BR "button yes"
and
.BR "button no" .
.SS Menu widgets
.BR menubar ", " menu ", " menuitem ", " separator
.SS Terminal and separators
.BR terminal ", " hseparator ", " vseparator
.SS Timers
.BR timer
.PP
Each widget exports its current value as a shell environment variable
(via
.BR eval )
when the dialog exits or an action requests a refresh.
.SH EXIT STATUS
gtk3sermo exits with status
.B 0
on normal termination. The exit value printed on standard output by an
EXIT action is a string, not a numeric exit code; the calling shell must
interpret it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=all
Enable
.BR g_debug ()
messages (verbose runtime tracing). Combined with
.B \-\-debug
this gives maximum diagnostic output.
.TP
.B GTK_DEBUG=interactive
Open the GTK Inspector inside the running window
.RB ( Ctrl\-Shift\-I ).
.TP
.B GTK_THEME
Override the GTK theme, e.g.
.BR GTK_THEME=Adwaita:dark .
.TP
.B HAPLO_NO_SHELL_FALLBACK
When set (to any value), refuse the
.B /bin/sh \-c
fallback used for
.RB < input >/< action >
commands that contain shell metacharacters, and fail closed instead. Commands
without shell metacharacters still run via direct
.BR exec ()
(no shell). Use this to harden gtk3sermo when rendering XML whose command
strings may come from a less-trusted source than the local script author (see
.B safe_exec.c
design note 1).
.TP
.B GTKDIALOG_PIXMAP_PATH
Colon\-separated list of directories in which gtk3sermo searches for image
files that are not found at the path given in the XML. It is consulted when
loading
.BR <pixmap> ,
window and button icons, and menu\-item images.
.TP
.B MAIN_DIALOG
Fallback source variable. When none of
.BR \-\-program ,
.BR \-\-file ,
.BR \-\-stdin ,
.B \-\-event\-driven
or
.B \-\-glade\-xml
is given, gtk3sermo reads the GUI description from the environment variable
named
.BR MAIN_DIALOG .
.SH EXAMPLES
Display a minimal dialog from a shell variable:
.PP
.nf
DIALOG='
<window title="Hello">
  <vbox>
    <text><label>Hello, world!</label></text>
    <button><label>OK</label><action>EXIT:ok</action></button>
  </vbox>
</window>'
gtk3sermo --program=DIALOG
.fi
.PP
Read a dialog description from a file and capture the output:
.PP
.nf
eval $(gtk3sermo --file=my_form.xml)
echo "User entered: $ENTRY"
.fi
.PP
Display a dialog from standard input (pipe):
.PP
.nf
cat my_form.xml | gtk3sermo --stdin
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/gtk3sermo
The gtk3sermo executable.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/gtk3sermo/examples/
Shell script examples for each supported widget type.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
.B gtk3sermo
is upward compatible with the original
.BR gtkdialog (1).
On installation,
.B make install
creates a
.B gtkdialog
symlink to
.B gtk3sermo
and a
.I gtkdialog.1
manual-page alias, so legacy dialogs (XML, command-line options, and the
.B \-\-program
environment-variable invocation) continue to work unchanged and print their
output in the historical
.IR NAME =\(dq value \(dq
form. Only gtk3sermo provides this alias, so there is no conflict between
packages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gtkdialog (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR zenity (1),
.BR yad (1)
.PP
Online documentation and widget reference:
